Chapter: List Comprehension Copy

Section: Entry

 tco-ensure-temps (codex/compiler/Emit/X86_64.codex) copies the caller's
 list with an identity comprehension before it pushes onto it, and this
 arm is what holds that copy honest. __list_snoc extends its argument in
 place when the argument is the topmost allocation, and base is a local
 literal with nothing allocated after it, so it is that shape. If the
 comprehension ever returned its input, the push would land in base and
 base-len would read 2. Replacing the comprehension with a plain
 reference to base is the control, and it does read 2.

  report : Integer -> Text
  report (x) =
   let base = [7]
   in let copied = for r in base -> r
   in let grown = list-push copied 9
   in "base-len=" & show (list-length base)
    & " grown-len=" & show (list-length grown)
    & " grown-head=" & show (list-at grown 0)

  opening : [Console] Integer
  opening = act
    (print-line-uni (report 0))
    0
  end
